# Roughly what each test file costs, in milliseconds, most expensive first.
#
# **A hint for packing, not a measurement, and being out of date only costs
# balance.** `scripts/parallel_pytest.py` packs files into one bundle per
# process and starts the heaviest first; with no idea what anything costs it
# packs round robin, and whichever bundle happens to collect the two slowest
# files sets the wall clock.
#
# It is committed because the runner's own table (`.pytest-file-times`) is
# gitignored and machine specific, so **CI never has one** - which is how the
# first parallel version of this ran drive in 148s on a two core runner, no
# better than the serial suite it replaced.
#
# Measured one file at a time on an idle 8-core laptop, so each figure includes
# about 1.3s of interpreter and import start-up. Regenerate with:
#   for f in drive/tests/test_*.py; do ... done   (see docs/testing.md)
